From: Ben Bangert <ben@groovie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: rk3576-rock-4d: set the HDMI DDC SDA falling delay

Without rockchip,sda-falling-delay-ns the RK3576 HDMI glue never enables
the GRF output-SDA delay (VO0_GRF_SOC_CON12), and EDID reads on the
ROCK 4D corrupt partway ("ddc read failed", "EDID block 0 checksum is
invalid"), leaving only fallback modes up to 1080p. 360 ns is the value
Rockchip's rk3576-evb1 and most other RK3576 boards use. With it the
full 256-byte EDID reads and a 4K TV comes up at 3840x2160p60.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
@@ -390,6 +390,7 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	cec-enable;
 	enable-gpios = <&gpio2 RK_PB0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	rockchip,sda-falling-delay-ns = <360>;
 };
 
 &hdmi_in_vp0 {
